# This project is developed on Windows and runs in Linux containers.
#
# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings. A .sh file checked out with CRLF fails
# inside Alpine with "no such file or directory" — pointing at the
# interpreter, not the script — because the kernel reads the shebang as
# "/bin/sh\r". It is a genuinely confusing hour to lose.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
docker/* text eol=lf

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the repository, let Git hand Windows
# whatever it prefers in the working tree.
* text=auto
